# SRG-APP-000150-AU-002320  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must use multifactor authentication for network
# access to non-privileged user accounts.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000150-AU-002320
group:           V-206462
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000766
control_rev5:    IA-2

contribution:    Splunk Web can require a client certificate, use it as the user
                 credential, and set the method by which the user identity is extracted
                 from that certificate, which is the product's share of multifactor network
                 logon for ordinary users; the Duo or RSA integration in
                 authentication.conf is the product's equivalent alternative route.

governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] requireClientCert equals true
check:           web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth equals true
check:           web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthMethod non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] certBasedUserAuthMethod https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] enableCertBasedUserAuth https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
vendor:          web.conf [settings] requireClientCert https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/authenticate-into-splunk-enterprise-using-hardware/configure-splunk-enterprise-to-use-a-common-access-card-for-authentication
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Issuance and possession of the PKI credential for each non-privileged
                 user, plus client-side reader and middleware
external:        Where Duo or RSA is used in place of PKI, vendor enrollment and policy
                 decide whether the second factor is demanded of each account
external:        The directory service that holds the account the extracted certificate
                 identity resolves to

citation:        SRG-APP-000150-AU-002320 check and fix text; web.conf.spec:120-132
                 (enableCertBasedUserAuth, default false), web.conf.spec:133-143
                 (certBasedUserAuthMethod values CommonName, EDIPI, PIV, no default),
                 web.conf.spec:151-167 (requireClientCert, default false);
                 authentication.conf.spec:87-99
finding:         Splunk requires no second authentication factor for network logon by
                 non-privileged accounts: neither the certificate path (web.conf
                 requireClientCert, enableCertBasedUserAuth and certBasedUserAuthMethod)
                 nor the vendor path (authentication.conf externalTwoFactorAuthVendor with
                 externalTwoFactorAuthSettings) is configured.
